# Linear story ticket

## How to use

Create or update an issue with `save_issue`. Put this body in `description`. A story is one user outcome. An epic is a project; use the epic template for that.

- `priority`: `1` Urgent, `2` High, `3` Medium, or `4` Low. Use `3` unless the user states otherwise.
- `addLabels`: an existing label from `list_issue_labels`.
- `blockedBy` and `relatedTo`: only issues the user names.
- `project`: the epic's project name, id, or `P-ENG-123` when the story belongs to one.
- `estimate`: set only when the user supplies a number.

Write a title that names the user goal. Delete any section below that does not apply.

## Body

```markdown
## User story

As a [person who uses this],
I want [goal],
so that [outcome].

## Description

[Constraint, dependency, or history the story needs. Omit when the user story is enough.]

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Given [precondition], when [action], then [outcome].
- [ ] [Another testable outcome.]
- [ ] [Edge case, when the story has one.]

## Out of scope

- [Outcome this story does not include.]
```
